WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.020 --> 00:00:02.200
Your AI doesn't read.

2
00:00:02.400 --> 00:00:03.420
Every word you type

3
00:00:03.420 --> 00:00:04.220
plots onto

4
00:00:04.220 --> 00:00:05.200
a hidden map.

5
00:00:05.440 --> 00:00:06.440
Most people imagine

6
00:00:06.440 --> 00:00:08.450
a giant digital dictionary.

7
00:00:08.690 --> 00:00:10.120
Instead, AI treats

8
00:00:10.120 --> 00:00:12.150
language as geometry.

9
00:00:12.460 --> 00:00:13.380
In 2013,

10
00:00:13.380 --> 00:00:14.260
Tomas Mikolov

11
00:00:14.260 --> 00:00:14.800
and his team

12
00:00:14.800 --> 00:00:17.280
at Google introduced Word2Vec.

13
00:00:17.520 --> 00:00:18.440
Their paper proved

14
00:00:18.440 --> 00:00:20.320
how context sets coordinates,

15
00:00:20.540 --> 00:00:21.320
and how math

16
00:00:21.320 --> 00:00:22.720
solves analogies.

17
00:00:23.080 --> 00:00:23.800
It starts with

18
00:00:23.800 --> 00:00:25.440
the distributional hypothesis.

19
00:00:25.680 --> 00:00:26.980
Words keeping similar company

20
00:00:26.980 --> 00:00:28.680
naturally drift together.

21
00:00:28.940 --> 00:00:30.100
Because "coffee" and "espresso"

22
00:00:30.100 --> 00:00:32.020
share verbs like brew,

23
00:00:32.240 --> 00:00:34.050
their dense embeddings cluster.

24
00:00:34.320 --> 00:00:35.380
This 3D particle cloud

25
00:00:35.380 --> 00:00:36.900
is only a projection.

26
00:00:37.320 --> 00:00:38.620
Word2Vec spans roughly

27
00:00:38.620 --> 00:00:39.850
300 dimensions,

28
00:00:39.850 --> 00:00:41.080
while modern models

29
00:00:41.080 --> 00:00:42.180
reach thousands.

30
00:00:42.540 --> 00:00:43.800
Yet proximity sparks

31
00:00:43.800 --> 00:00:45.250
a stranger twist.

32
00:00:45.520 --> 00:00:46.420
Relationships point

33
00:00:46.420 --> 00:00:48.000
along fixed directions.

34
00:00:48.240 --> 00:00:49.060
Take King,

35
00:00:49.340 --> 00:00:50.520
subtract Man,

36
00:00:50.780 --> 00:00:51.450
add Woman.

37
00:00:51.720 --> 00:00:53.250
You land beside Queen.

38
00:00:53.520 --> 00:00:54.460
Paris minus France

39
00:00:54.460 --> 00:00:55.220
plus Italy

40
00:00:55.220 --> 00:00:56.750
steers straight to Rome.

41
00:00:57.000 --> 00:00:57.820
Meaning behaves

42
00:00:57.820 --> 00:00:58.950
like a compass.

43
00:00:59.200 --> 00:01:00.340
Therefore, full sentences

44
00:01:00.340 --> 00:01:01.850
follow those bearings.

45
00:01:02.240 --> 00:01:03.060
Today's models blend

46
00:01:03.060 --> 00:01:03.660
word vectors

47
00:01:03.660 --> 00:01:04.980
to pinpoint your prompt.

48
00:01:05.220 --> 00:01:05.920
Rephrase it,

49
00:01:06.100 --> 00:01:06.900
and its position

50
00:01:06.900 --> 00:01:07.900
barely shifts.

51
00:01:08.240 --> 00:01:09.100
That overlap lets

52
00:01:09.100 --> 00:01:10.820
software infer intent.

53
00:01:11.160 --> 00:01:12.300
Letters are only

54
00:01:12.300 --> 00:01:13.060
the surface.

55
00:01:13.340 --> 00:01:14.300
Once language turns

56
00:01:14.300 --> 00:01:15.340
into geometry,

57
00:01:15.480 --> 00:01:16.800
machines understand ideas

58
00:01:16.800 --> 00:01:17.680
by measuring

59
00:01:17.680 --> 00:01:18.680
where they live.
